        "text": "Before my first visit, I assumed I'd need a camera to record what I saw. But the group leader said that wasn't necessary. She suggested bringing binoculars instead, so I could see birds on the far bank without disturbing them. The group has some you can borrow, but I bought a small pair. They're easy to carry, and I use them on walks with my family now, too."
