        "text": "We normally meet at nine, outside the café near the station, and walk to the river together. There are several paths down to the water, and the first time I went alone, I took the wrong one. The easiest way is to follow the path past the old stone bridge. Once you've gone under it, you'll see a wide grassy area where we leave our bags. It's much quieter there than it is near the road."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Hannah",
        "text": "One of our jobs is to find young trees that might need protecting. Last winter, some of them were damaged when the river rose after heavy rain. Now, when we find a tree that needs attention, we tie an orange ribbon around it. Someone suggested using paint, but we decided against that because it could harm the tree. Later, another team comes along and puts a small fence around it."
