        "text": "We also collect information about the river itself. At first, I thought the most important thing would be its depth, especially after rain. But the measurement we take every week is the water temperature. We check it in the same place each time, so that the results can be compared. Changes can affect the animals living in the river, even if the water still looks clean to us."
      },
